 "status": "complete",
 "note": "On held-out Sasha the shipped Mac 2B scores 89.7% on 175 known gaps (pages exact 37.4%), against the teacher's 67.4% and its bf16 source's 89.1%. The source's pages exact is 46.6%: similar gap accuracy can leave different long documents wrong, and these single runs do not rank quantizations. The Illustrated Review and SC0122 are trained-on diagnostics for the students, not evidence of generalization. SC0122's supported comparison is its owner-ruled disagreement gaps plus controls weighted to the agreed strata; document-exact scores there remain conditional on tag/teacher-drafted truth. Gemini 3.7 Flash scores 96.0% on held-out Sasha (pages exact 82.2%); paired against the Mac 2B it is 6.3 points ahead on gap accuracy (sign test p 0.019), and far ahead on whole documents. On the Illustrated Review it merges 40 article gaps, because g1 still asks for the full magazine issue (W46.seg-magazine-rule-redo), so its pages exact there is no test of reading ability. Across three cloud offsets, no-check exact pages range 83.0%\u201385.2% and checks per 100 pages 25.9\u201327.3; the 3.8-fitted flag level is unchanged."
}
